{
  "description": "Pane layout rules shared by the Mac (PaneLayoutTree, PaneLayoutTreeMutation, PaneLayoutState, PaneLayoutMinimumSize, PaneLayoutGeometry) and the desktop client (soyeht_client::layout). Trees are the protocol layout nodes. Both pass every case. Where a pane goes that the tree does not list (`arrange`) is shared too: by role, primary panes left to right and auxiliary panes stacked on the right. Each case gives the floors to weigh with (the file's floor for a kind it does not list), a stored layout and the live panes in workspace order.",
